#!/usr/bin/env python3
# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
Architecture:
  - One long-lived Chrome process, owns a single --user-data-dir (shared profile).
  - Remote debugging on 127.0.0.1:$BUA_CDP_PORT (default 9222).
  - Each OpenClaw session id (sid) is mapped to a Chrome windowId AND a
    persisted activeTargetId (the tab bua treats as the sid's active page).
  - Each session also keeps a stable `tabsOrder` — an ordered list of
    targetIds that belong to the session's window, enabling per-session
    references like T1/T2 for the `bua tabs` command family.
  - High-level actions (snapshot/act/click/...) are delegated to `agent-browser
    --cdp <port> ...` after activating the persisted activeTargetId. If that
    target has vanished (closed / crashed), bua falls back to the newest
    non-blank tab in the window and persists the new choice.
  - Cookies / localStorage / auth are shared across all windows because they
    all live in the same Chrome profile.

No external Python deps: an embedded minimal WebSocket client speaks CDP.
"""
from __future__ import annotations
